            "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"360\" height=\"220\" viewBox=\"0 0 360 220\"><g stroke=\"#dbe3ed\" stroke-width=\"1\"><path d=\"M35 35V95M75 35V95M115 35V95M155 35V95M195 35V95M235 35V95M275 35V95M315 35V95M35 40H155M35 65H155M35 90H155M195 40H315M195 65H315M195 90H315M35 130V190M75 130V190M115 130V190M155 130V190M195 130V190M235 130V190M275 130V190M315 130V190M35 135H155M35 160H155M35 185H155M195 135H315M195 160H315M195 185H315\"/></g><g stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"><path d=\"M35 65H155M95 35V95M195 65H315M255 35V95M35 160H155M95 130V190M195 160H315M255 130V190\"/></g><g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.7\"><path d=\"M42 37 C58 37 67 90 92 90 C118 90 125 38 150 38\"/><path d=\"M202 39 C224 39 228 85 252 68 C276 50 286 89 309 91\"/><path d=\"M42 184 C65 184 69 138 94 150 C119 162 130 180 150 135\"/><path d=\"M202 184 C222 184 231 137 254 151 C276 166 291 137 309 136\"/></g><g fill=\"#334155\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\"><text x=\"35\" y=\"28\">A</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"28\">B</text><text x=\"35\" y=\"123\">C</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"123\">D</text></g></svg>"
          },
          "options": [
            "Diagram A",
            "Diagram B",
            "Diagram C",
            "Diagram D"
          ],
          "answer": 1,
          "hint": "A cubic with a negative leading coefficient rises on the left and falls on the right. It has opposite end behaviour.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "A cubic has odd degree, so its two ends point in opposite directions.",
              "work": "For large |x|, the leading term −3x³ controls the graph."
            },
            {
              "explain": "Because the leading coefficient is negative, the left end rises and the right end falls.",
              "work": "x → −∞ ⇒ y → +∞;  x → +∞ ⇒ y → −∞"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Only diagram B has this end behaviour and a cubic shape.",
              "work": "Choose Diagram B."
            }
