      "title": "The remainder theorem and factor theorem",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "jrhy2008-q27",
          "type": "mc",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "stem": "The remainder when \\(3x^3-7x^2+2x+4\\) is divided by \\((x-3)\\) is:",
          "options": [
            "\\(-28\\)",
            "\\(-137\\)",
            "\\(137\\)",
            "\\(28\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 3,
          "hint": "By the remainder theorem, the remainder equals \\(P(3)\\).",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "By the remainder theorem, substitute \\(x=3\\) into the polynomial.",
              "work": "\\(P(3) = 3(3)^3-7(3)^2+2(3)+4 = 3(27)-7(9)+6+4\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Evaluate.",
              "work": "\\(= 81-63+6+4 = 28\\)"
            }
          ],
          "meta": {
            "source": "James Ruse AHS 2008 Year 10 Half-Yearly",
            "school": "James Ruse Agricultural High School",
            "examType": "Half-Yearly",
            "grade": "10"
          },
          "xp": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "jr2013-qFb",
          "type": "mc",
          "stem": "(b) When the polynomial \\(P(x)=x^3-ax^2+x\\) is divided by \\((x-3)\\), the remainder is 12. Find the remainder when \\(P(x)\\) is divided by \\((x+1)\\).",
          "options": [
            "\\(2\\)",
            "\\(-2\\)",
            "\\(4\\)",
            "\\(-4\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 3,
          "hint": "Use the remainder theorem: substitute \\(x=3\\) to find \\(a\\), then substitute \\(x=-1\\) into \\(P(x)\\) to find the required remainder.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "By the remainder theorem, \\(P(3)=12\\). Substitute and solve for \\(a\\).",
              "work": "\\(P(3) = 27-9a+3 = 30-9a = 12\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Solve for \\(a\\).",
              "work": "\\(9a=18 \\Rightarrow a=2\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Now find the remainder when \\(P(x)\\) is divided by \\((x+1)\\), which by the remainder theorem is \\(P(-1)\\).",
              "work": "\\(P(-1) = (-1)^3-2(-1)^2+(-1) = -1-2-1\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Evaluate.",
              "work": "\\(P(-1) = -4\\)"
            }
          ],
          "xp": 2,
          "difficulty": "hard",
          "meta": {
            "source": "James Ruse AHS 2013 Year 10 Yearly",
            "school": "James Ruse Agricultural High School",
            "examType": "Yearly",
            "grade": "10",
            "sourceSection": "Section F",
            "sourcePart": "b"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "abb-y10-2025-t4-e1-q3",
          "type": "mc",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "stem": "Solve 3x³ − 6x² − 15x + 18 = 0.",
          "options": [
            "x=−2,1,3",
            "x=−3,1,2",
            "x=−2,−1,3",
            "x=−1,2,3"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "hint": "Factor out 3, test x=1, and factor the remaining quadratic.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Remove the common factor 3.",
              "work": "x³−2x²−5x+6=0"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Test x=1 and divide by (x−1).",
              "work": "1−2−5+6=0;\nx³−2x²−5x+6=(x−1)(x²−x−6)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Factor and solve.",
              "work": "(x−1)(x−3)(x+2)=0; x=1,3,−2"
            }
          ],
          "keyPoints": [
            {
              "text": "Solve 3x³ − 6x² − 15x + 18 = 0",
              "note": "Take out 3, find a simple root, then factor the remaining quadratic."
            }
          ],
